  Quote of the Week:

  Pope Julius II, in reply to Michelangelo, who had asked which of his 
artistic tools the Pope would like to try (1506):
  "Nay, give me a sword, for I am no scholar."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  In spring, Shauku prepared her armies to defend Namibia and the 
surrounding provinces.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Shauku Endbringer for this year.

  Josh the gentle (#3) Treated with Shauku Endbringer, but Shauku did not 
react to his friendly noises.  It is hoped that next year, both Kings will 
see the wisdom of Treating.


  Here is the financial report for Shauku's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 0 gold in revenue.  0 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  0 
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Shauku was left with 17 gold in 
the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Marlon
To: Shauku

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season I prepared to quench my thirst for 
adventure.  I prepared my armies to defend Kenya and the surrounding 
provinces.

  Thy humble servant,   Marlon


